 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Permits commercial feed manufacturers to use the term \"human food grade\" for certain pet food if it conforms to certain state and federal standards.",
 "title": "Relates to using the term  human food grade  for certain pet food",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A4570",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A4570-2021",
     "printNo": "A4570",
     "session": 2021,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 101\n \nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nAssembly Bill Number 4570-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the agriculture and markets law, in relation to\n      using the term \"human food grade\" for certain pet food\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would establish a standard for  pet  food  manufacturers  to\nlabel  and  advertise their products as \"human grade food,\" and prohibit\nmanufacturers whose products do not meet such standard from  using  this\nterm.\n \n  The Department of Agriculture and Markets (AGM) regulates the manufac-\nture  and  distribution of pet food and pet treats in the State. AGM has\nestablished labeling guidelines requiring that manufacturers marketing a\nproduct as human grade be able to substantiate that each  ingredient  is\nsuitable  for  human  consumption, appropriately stored and handled, and\nmanufactured in a facility licensed to produce human food by the  appro-\npriate  authority.  Nationally, the Association of American Feed Control\nOfficials, through the Food and Drug Administration, has provided  guid-\nance  covering  this  topic.  Additionally,  AGM has taken steps against\nthose manufacturers making dubious human-grade claims on their pet  food\nregistration application.\n \n  While  I understand and support the intent of the bill, deviating from\nthe federal guidelines and implementing the New  York-specific  approach\nwill  be  costly  and overburdensome for AGM to implement. Given current\nregulations and enforcement, there will be no additional gain to  public\nor pet health.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 101,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2022
   }
  ],
  "size": 1
 },
